\input{graphs/results/appendix_rq2_ce_identity}
The results were obtained using the FELICS reference implementation and the adapted baseline implementation of Matton et al.~\cite{mattonWalkTalkMeasuring2024}, following the methodology specified in Chapter~\ref{ch:evaluation_methodology}. The evaluation covers three datasets and two models. The experiment outputs and their interpretation are documented in Appendix~\ref{app:reproducibility}. The results provide an overview of the empirical behavior of both metrics and address the four research questions introduced in Section~\ref{sec:research_questions}, followed by the case study on the MedQA example. The corresponding hypothesis tests were conducted as specified in Section~\ref{sec:analysis_procedures}, and their outcomes are summarized in research-hypothesis boxes.

The chapter begins with an overview of how dataset-level causal effects and faithfulness change when joint interventions are introduced. It then examines the oracle behavior on natural-language and tabular datasets before addressing each research question through statistical tests and selected figures. Four selected coalition effects and the case study conclude the chapter. Figures for the dataset--model combinations that are not shown in this chapter are collected in Appendix~\ref{app:additional-result-visualizations}.
